    {
      "id": "claim_dc5ba2ef2cd34708898d94a3dee4ff5f",
      "statement": "The audio player implements automatic error recovery with exponential backoff (getRetryDelay = base * 2^count giving 1s/2s/4s, MAX_RETRIES = 3): an error event sets hasError and calls scheduleAudioRetry only when wasPlayingBeforeError and navigator.onLine; each attempt shows a persistent 'Versuch n/3 in x s' buffering pill; retryAudio clears hasError, sets isAutoRetry (so the next error does not reset the count), reloads and plays; canplay clears the retry state; after the count is exhausted showExhaustedText shows 'Stream nicht erreichbar' for 6s and leaves a persistent error dot. The offline event clears the pending timer and message while keeping the count; the online event triggers an immediate retryAudio with the count clamped to MAX_RETRIES - 1 when exhausted.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/js/player-core.js#L206-L238",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49bbb8c840c9693b1605fe824b8647dadbc9536e89a48db9b5ebeb493f383425:"
        },
